{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1792654251.9579735, "id": "87331179f082", "tool_call_id": "call_00_UD4JoymbIS60qycWqCRn3353", "content": "OK: command succeeded\nstdout:\ndiff --git a/diff_env/target.py b/diff_env/target.py\nindex 864de21..d269604 100644\n--- a/diff_env/target.py\n+++ b/diff_env/target.py\n@@ -60,13 +60,13 @@ class BodyMotion(nn.Module):\n                 2 * math.pi * yaw_freq.unsqueeze(1) * t\n             )\n \n-        pitch = pitch_0.unsqueeze(1)\n+        pitch = pitch_0.unsqueeze(1).expand(-1, sln)\n         if pitch_amp.abs().sum() > 0:\n             pitch = pitch + pitch_amp.unsqueeze(1) * torch.sin(\n                 2 * math.pi * pitch_freq.unsqueeze(1) * t\n             )\n \n-        roll = roll_0.unsqueeze(1)\n+        roll = roll_0.unsqueeze(1).expand(-1, sln)\n         if roll_amp.abs().sum() > 0:\n             roll = roll + roll_amp.unsqueeze(1) * torch.sin(\n                 2 * math.pi * roll_freq.unsqueeze(1) * t\n@@ -87,8 +87,8 @@ class ArmorLayout(nn.Module):\n         self,\n         n_armors: int,\n         radius: torch.Tensor,\n-        radius_offsets: torch.Tensor = None,\n-        height_offsets: torch.Tensor = None,\n+        radius_offsets: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n+        height_offsets: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n     ):\n         device = radius.device\n         bsz = radius.shape[0]\n@@ -109,14 +109,17 @@ class ArmorLayout(nn.Module):\n             / n_armors\n         )\n \n-        local_x = radius.unsqueeze(-1) * torch.cos(theta)\n-        local_y = radius.unsqueeze(-1) * torch.sin(theta)\n+        r_eff = radius.unsqueeze(-1) + radius_offsets\n+        local_x = r_eff * torch.cos(theta)\n+        local_y = r_eff * torch.sin(theta)\n         local_z = height_offsets\n         local_positions = torch.stack([local_x, local_y, local_z], dim=-1)\n \n-        yaws = theta.unsqueeze(0)\n+        yaws = theta.unsqueeze(0).expand(bsz, -1)\n+        # vertical armor: width tangential, height up, normal radial outward\n         zeros = torch.zeros_like(yaws)\n-        local_rotations = euler_to_rotmat(yaws, zeros, zeros)\n+        half_pi = torch.full_like(yaws, math.pi / 2)\n+        local_rotations = euler_to_rotmat(yaws + half_pi, zeros, half_pi)\n \n         w2 = self.armor_width / 2\n         h2 = self.armor_height / 2\n@@ -135,13 +138,13 @@ class ArmorLayout(nn.Module):\n \n \n class TargetMotion(nn.Module):\n-    def __init__(self, armor_width: float = 0.02, armor_height: float = 0.06):\n+    def __init__(self, armor_width: float = 0.12, armor_height: float = 0.06):\n         super().__init__()\n         self.body_motion = BodyMotion()\n         self.armor_layout = ArmorLayout(armor_width, armor_height)\n \n     def forward(self, t, mode=\"static\", **params):\n-        bsz, sln = t.shape\n+        bsz, _ = t.shape\n         device = t.device\n \n         if mode in (\"static\", \"constant_velocity\"):\n@@ -162,10 +165,20 @@ class TargetMotion(nn.Module):\n         body_pos = body[\"positions\"]\n         body_rot = body[\"rotations\"]\n \n-        local_pos, local_rot, corners_local = self.armer_layout(\n+        local_pos, local_rot, corners_local = self.armor_layout(\n             n_armors, radius, radius_offsets, height_offsets\n         )\n \n         centers = body_pos.unsqueeze(2) + torch.einsum(\n-            \"btij,bnj->btni\", body_rot, local_pos\n+            \"btij,bmj->btmi\", body_rot, local_pos\n         )\n+        world_rot = torch.einsum(\"btik,bmkj->btmij\", body_rot, local_rot)\n+        corners = centers.unsqueeze(-2) + torch.einsum(\n+            \"btmij,cj->btmci\", world_rot, corners_local\n+        )\n+        # facing direction of each plate: local +Z is the plate normal\n+        normal_local = torch.tensor([0.0, 0.0, 1.0], device=device, dtype=radius.dtype)\n+        world_normal = torch.einsum(\"btmij,j->btmi\", world_rot, normal_local)\n+        armor_yaws = torch.atan2(world_normal[..., 1], world_normal[..., 0])\n+\n+        return {\"corners\": corners, \"centers\": centers, \"armor_yaws\": armor_yaws}\n", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1792654263.9822812, "id": "9fd6593ea98c", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_NeuE7mE3mLjHYNhn3Myu7164", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"grep -n -i \\\"armor\\\\|visual\\\" README.md | head -20; git status --short\"}"}], "reasoning": "Wait, there's a subtle bug in the einsum for corners: `\"btmij,cj->btmci\"` — world_rot is (b,t,m,3,3), corners_local is (c,3) where c=4. Output (b,t,m,c,i) fine. But `corners = centers.unsqueeze(-2)` gives (b,t,m,1,3) broadcasting with (b,t,m,4,3) ✓.\n\nNote: the corners ordering: corners_local rows are corners, shape (4,3), so `\"btmij,cj->btmci\"` maps j→i. Good.\n\nAlso `armor_yaws` is the world-frame yaw; fine.\n\nPotential issue: `radius_offsets` has shape (bsz, n_armors) and r_eff (bsz,n_armors) ✓.\n\nNow the einsum `\"btij,bmj->btmi\"` with local_pos (bsz,n,3): if bsz=2, local_pos shape (2,n,3) matches b. In the original, local_pos was (bsz,n,3) and einsum used b differently (\"bnj\" with b as second dim). Now \"bmj\": for bsz>1, both b and m indices need matching sizes: body_rot (b,t,3,3), local_pos (b,n,3) → \"bmj\" means dim0=b (size bsz) and m=n. This forces local_pos's first dim == bsz ✓. But when bsz==1 and n_armors=4 (local_pos (1,4,3)): \"bmj\" → b=1, m=4 ✓. However, if bsz>1 but local_pos's leading dim is 1 (not expanded), it fails. local_pos = stack of r_eff * cos(theta) → r_eff (bsz,n) so leading dim bsz ✓.\n\nNow double check: does `zeros` param in `euler_to_rotmat` accept a zero tensor and half_pi tensor? yes.\n\nVisual check of the image: it would be good to look at the actual PNG. I can't view images, but I could analyze the camera panel region for line positions. The earlier pixel check gave non-white 345k which includes panels/labels. A sanity check: crop the camera view panel? Hard.\n\nAlternative: render only the camera panel at 1280x1024 with axes off and check that front plates are filled rectangles of expected pixel size. That was in