nated. Fine.\n\nBut note the right panel (camera view) has \"axis-coloured\" pixels from armor colors — not an issue in reality.\n\nLet me instead verify the triads in the 3D panels programmatically: check that the world triad directions are drawn correctly. Hard via pixels. Alternative: trust the `draw_frame` implementation and verify the math (already did: R columns).\n\nBut one thing to verify visually: labels and limits. Let me view the whole figure as a downscaled ASCII by luminance to see the layout. Or better: check the axes content bounding boxes by rendering only data (no text)? Not needed.\n\nHmm, I realize the mid panel has the body triad at the center and armor triads around; the ASCII shows clusters at various positions. Plausible.\n\nHowever, I notice in the left panel ASCII, the origin triad at top-left and body triad at bottom-right — good.\n\nNow, about the target.py discrepancy: I need to decide. Let me look at the plot: with tangential normals, the camera view shows A1/A3 (side plates at θ=90/270) facing the camera... Let me compute the current facing cos values."}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1792656369.430982, "id": "43696be9cf8d", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cat > /tmp/check_current.py <<\\\"PYEOF\\\"\\nimport sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\".\\\")\\nimport numpy as np, torch\\nfrom diff_env.target import TargetMotion\\nfrom scripts.visualize_target import camera_rotation, project\\n\\nout = TargetMotion()(torch.zeros(1, 1), \\\"complex\\\",\\n                     p0=torch.tensor([[3.0, 0.0, 0.5]]),\\n                     n_armors=4, radius=torch.tensor([0.3]))\\nc = out[\\\"corners\\\"][0, 0].numpy(); ce = out[\\\"centers\\\"][0, 0].numpy()\\nR = out[\\\"armor_rotations\\\"][0, 0].numpy()\\nn = np.cross(c[:, 1] - c[:, 0], c[:, 3] - c[:, 0]); n /= np.linalg.norm(n, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\\ncos = (n * (np.array([0.0, 0.0, 0.5]) - ce)).sum(-1)\\nu, v, z = project(c, camera_rotation(0), np.array([0.0, 0.0, 0.5]), 800, 800, 640, 512)\\nfor m in range(4):\\n    print(f\\\"A{m}: center {np.round(ce[m], 2)}  normal {np.round(n[m], 2)}  \\\"\\n          f\\\"depth {z[m].mean():.2f} bbox {np.ptp(u[m]):.1f}x{np.ptp(v[m]):.1f} cos {cos[m]:+.2f}\\\")\\nprint(\\\"armor_yaws deg:\\\", np.degrees(out[\\\"armor_yaws\\\"][0, 0].numpy()))\\nPYEOF\\n.venv/bin/python /tmp/check_current.py\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_Me9XgRWVtMK2SdnBukwK8119", "ui": {"group": null, "chip": "name", "summary": "", "preview": "command", "header": "", "form": "block", "body": "text", "collapse": "never", "highlight": "", "chrome": "", "mutates": true, "undo": false}, "path_arg": ""}
