{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1793176354.8689623, "id": "d1aa8fc0ef3b", "tool_call_id": "call_00_KQwKPyqkAw3cU4VN9s7s0050", "content": "scripts/visualize_target.py:\n  Line 46: def set_limits(ax, points, pad=0.1):\n  Line 51:     ax.set_xlim(mid[0] - half, mid[0] + half)\n  Line 52:     ax.set_ylim(mid[1] - half, mid[1] + half)\n  Line 62: def update(index: int, out: dict, args, fig, ax, ax2, ax_img):\n  Line 68:     ax.clear()\n  Line 69:     ax2.clear()\n  Line 70:     ax_img.clear()\n  Line 91:     set_limits(ax, np.vstack([corners.reshape(-1, 3), cam_pos, np.zeros(3)]))\n  Line 101:     set_limits(ax2, np.vstack([corners.reshape(-1, 3), body]), pad=0.15)\n  Line 116:     ax_img.set_xlim(u.min() - pad, u.max() + pad)\n  Line 117:     ax_img.set_ylim(v.max() + pad, v.min() - pad)     # v grows downwards\n  Line 118:     ax_img.set_aspect(\"equal\")\n  Line 150:     out = TargetMotion()(\n  Line 166:     ax     = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 1, projection=\"3d\")\n  Line 167:     ax2    = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 2, projection=\"3d\")\n  Line 168:     ax_img = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 3)", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1793176375.5368826, "id": "fb06b4a14e4f", "content": "## 先说结论：有三处在每帧重新计算窗口，导致比例尺跳动\n\n| 位置 | 代码 | 每帧变化的原因 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 第 91 行 | `set_limits(ax, corners + cam_pos + origin)` | 装甲旋转后点云的 bbox 中心值和边长都会变，因此整个场景轻微地缩放并平移 |\n| 第 101 行 | `set_limits(ax2, corners + body)` | 同上，而且 close-up 面板对变化更敏感 |\n| 第 116–117 行 | `ax_img.set_xlim(u.min(), u.max())` | 直接按投影 bbox 计算，因此每米对应的像素数会随正面、侧面切换而变；再加上第 118 行 `set_aspect(\"equal\")` 会把由 box 控制的可调维度也一起重新调整，导致面板几何每帧“呼吸” |\n\n关键点：如果把整个轨迹在 `out[\"corners\"]` 中预先算好了（形状是 `(T, M, 4, 3)`），那么完全不需要逐帧重新计算 bbox；只要取**整段轨迹的并集**计算一次即可。\n\n---\n\n## 方案 A（推荐：改动最小，只需把“每帧重算”换成“每帧重新应用固定常量”）\n\n### 1. 把 `set_limits`（第 46–57 行）拆成“计算内存 + 应用”\n\n```python\ndef cube_limits(points, pad=0.1):\n    \"\"\"一整段轨迹的联合 bbox -> (xmin, xmax, ymin, ymax, zmin, zmax)。\"\"\"\n    pts = np.reshape(points, (-1, 3))\n    lo, hi = pts.min(0), pts.max(0)\n    mid, half = (lo + hi) / 2, (hi - lo).max() / 2 + pad\n    return (mid[0] - half, mid[0] + half,\n            mid[1] - half, mid[1] + half,\n            mid[2] - half, mid[2] + half)\n\n\ndef apply_cube(ax, lim):\n    ax.set_xlim(lim[0], lim[1])\n    ax.set_ylim(lim[2], lim[3])\n    ax.set_zlim(lim[4], lim[5])\n    ax.set_box_aspect((1.0, 1.0, 1.0))\n```\n\n### 2. 在 `main` 里、`out = TargetMotion()(...)` 之后（约第 157 行）加这一段\n\n```python\n    w, h = args.image_size\n    cam_pos = np.array([0.0, 0.0, args.height])\n    body = np.array([args.distance, 0.0, args.height])\n    R_wc = camera_rotation(args.cam_yaw)\n\n    allc = out[\"corners\"][0].numpy()                    # (T, M, 4, 3) 整段轨迹\n    ua, va, _ = project(allc, R_wc, cam_pos, args.fx, args.fx, w / 2, h / 2)\n\n    fixed = {\n        \"ax\":  cube_limits(np.vstack([allc.reshape(-1, 3), cam_pos, np.zeros(3)]), 0.1),\n        \"ax2\": cube_limits(np.vstack([allc.reshape(-1, 3), body]), 0.15),\n    }\n\n    ppm = args.fx / args.distance        # 目标深度处的 px/m，常量\n    half_m = args.radius + 0.25          # 视野半宽（米），与旋转无关\n    cu, cv = ua.mean(), va.mean()\n    fixed[\"img\"] = (cu - half_m * ppm, cu + half_m * ppm,\n                    cv + half_m * ppm, cv - half_m * ppm)   # v 向下\n```\n\n注意，`half_m` 是**用米来定义视野**，不按像素定义，因此它与旋转、bbox 都无关；这才是真正“比例尺不动”的做法。3 m 处 `ppm ≈ 267 px/m`，`half_m=0.55` 大约对应 293 px 宽的面板。\n\n### 3. 在 `update` 里删掉第 91、101、115–117 行，改成在 `clear()` 之后重新应用常量\n\n```python\n    apply_cube(ax, fixed[\"ax\"])\n    apply_cube(ax2, fixed[\"ax2\"])\n    ax_img.set_xlim(fixed[\"img\"][0], fixed[\"img\"][1])\n    ax_img.set_ylim(fixed[\"img\"][2], fixed[\"img\"][3])\n    ax_img.set_aspect(\"equal\")\n```\n\n同时把函数签名和调用改成 `update(index, out, args, fig, ax, ax2, ax_img, fixed)` / `update(i, out, args, fig, ax, ax2, ax_img, fixed)`。\n\n> 为什么必须放在 `clear()` 之后：第 68–70 行的 `clear()` 会清掉之前的 `set_xlim/set_ylim`，并将其恢复为 autoscale。因此“只设一次”的前提是**不 clear**（见方案 B）；在会 clear 的结构里，就必须每帧把**同一组数字**重新应用一次。数字相同，画面就不会跳动。\n\n### 4. 顺手把每帧不变的文字移出 `update`\n\n`set_title` / `suptitle`（第 119、121、122、124 行附近）在帧与帧之间完全一样，可以放到 `main` 里设置一次，或改成一个固定显示 `f\"{ppm:.0f} px/m\"` 的比例尺标注；这样可以同时避免布局抖动，并减少一些渲染开销。\n\n---\n\n## 方案 B（更彻底：不 clear，只更新坐标数值）\n\n每帧调用 `clear()` 再重建，是让限制（limits）无法持久保留的根本原因。把 `update` 拆成“建一次 / 改数值”后，比例尺就自然固定了：\n\n```python\n# 建一次（在 main 里，frame 0 的数据）\nlines3d  = [ax.plot([], [], [], color=c, lw=2)[0] for c in AXIS_COLORS]\nplates3d = [ax.plot([], [], [], color=\"#666666\", lw=1.0)[0] for _ in range(4)]\npatches  = [mpl.patches.Polygon(np.zeros((4, 2)), closed=True) for _ in range(4)]\nlabels   = [ax_img.text(0, 0, f\"A{m}\", fontsize=8) for m in range(4)]\n\n# 每帧（只换数据，绝不碰 xlim/ylim/aspect/title）\nline.set_data_3d(xs, ys, zs)     # Line3D\npatch.set_xy(np.c_[uu, vv])      # 2D 多边形\nlabel.set_position((uu.mean(), vv.mean()))\n```\n\n几点实测上重要的细节：\n\n- `Line3D.set_data_3d()`（`mplot3d/art3d.py:319`）只设置 `self._verts3d` 并标记 `stale = True`，**不会**触发 `_request_autoscale_view()`，所以不会被重新缩放；而 `ax.plot()` 每帧添加新 Line 时会触发 autoscale，这正是现在必须每帧重新应用 limit 的原因。\n- 建 artist 之后，只调用一次 `apply_cube(...)` / `set_xlim/ylim` / `set_aspect(\"equal\")`，再设置 `ax.set_autoscale_on(False)` 作为保险。\n- 附带收益：不再重建 ticks、panes 和 text，单帧渲染可以从 150–300 ms 降到几十毫秒；这正好配合你上一版按实际时间跳帧的改法，掉帧会明显减少。\n- 3D 面板的 `set_box_aspect((1,1,1))` 也只需要设置一次；如果每帧都设置，虽然不会造成乱跳，但也没有必要。\n\n## 方案 C（折中：保留 clear，但把三个面板的限制都设为常量）\n\n这种方式就是方案 A 中的第 3 步，不把 artist 预先建好；改动只有 6 行左右，先解决画面跳动，性能问题留到后面处理。**如果你想尽快看到效果，可以先做这一步。**\n\n---\n\n## 改完怎么验证“不跳了”\n\n在 `update` 末尾打印一行内容，查看这三个量是否恒定（只要还在变化，就说明某处仍在重新计算 limits）：\n\n```python\nprint(np.ptp(u).round(1), np.ptp(v).round(1),\n      ax.get_xlim(), ax_img.get_xlim())\n```\n\n- 改之前：`np.ptp(u)` 会在正面宽和侧棱窄之间来回变化（大约 190→240 px，也就是 20% 以上的比例尺跳动）；`ax.get_xlim()` 的四个数每帧都不相同。\n- 改之后：`np.ptp(u)` 仍然会变（这是目标实际投影尺寸，本来就应该变），但 `ax.get_xlim()` / `ax_img.get_xlim()` 必须每帧完全一致。\n\n再检查 2D 面板的物理比例尺：把 `--distance 3` 改成 `5`，`ppm` 应从 267 掉到 160，而画面中板的像素宽度也应同比缩小；这说明“固定的是比例尺，不是包围盒”。\n\n---\n\n我目前处于 chat（只读）模式，上面是分析和可直接粘贴的补丁。要我把它写进 `scripts/visualize_target.py`，即采用方案 A 的 `cube_limits/apply_cube` + `fixed` 字典，并把 `ppm` 标在标题上，然后跑一遍 `--distance 3` 和 `--distance 5`，对比输出尺寸；那就切到 work mode，我立刻开始。", "tool_calls": [], "reasoning": "Now write the answer. Three per-frame limit recomputations:\n- line 91 (panel1 3D)\n- line 101 (panel2 3D)\n- lines 116–117 (panel3 2D)\nAnd because of `clear()` at 68–70, limits must be re-applied after clear (or stop clearing).\n\nGood approach options:\n\n### 方案 A（推荐，最小改动）: 一次性算好，update 只\"重贴\"常量\n1. add helper `limits(points, pad)` returning the 6 numbers (refactor `set_limits` into `cube_limits` + `apply_limits`).\n2. in main, compute union over all frames → `fixed` dict; also image window from a fixed px/m.\n3. in update, after clear, apply `fixed` (no recompute).\n\nGive concrete code:\n\n```python\ndef cube_limits(points, pad=0.1):\n    pts = np.reshape(points, (-1, 3))\n    lo, hi = pts.min(0), pts.max(0)\n    mid, half = (lo + hi) / 2, (hi - lo).max() / 2 + pad\n    return (mid[0] - half, mid[0] + half,\n            mid[1] - half, mid[1] + half,\n            mid[2] - half, mid[2] + half)\n\n\ndef apply_cube(ax, lim):\n    ax.set_xlim(lim[0], lim[1]); ax.set_ylim(lim[2], lim[3]); ax.set_zlim(lim[4], lim[5])\n    ax.set_box_aspect((1.0, 1.0, 1.0))\n```\n\nIn main (after `out = ...`, line ~157):\n```python\n    w, h = args.image_size\n    cam_pos = np.array([0.0, 0.0, args.height])\n    body = np.array([args.distance, 0.0, args.height])\n    R_wc = camera_rotation(args.cam_yaw)\n    allc = out[\"corners\"][0].numpy()                    # (T, M, 4, 3)\n    ua, va, _ = project(allc, R_wc, cam_pos, args.fx, args.fx, w / 2, h / 2)\n\n    fixed = {\n        \"ax\":  cube_limits(np.vstack([allc.reshape(-1, 3), cam_pos, np.zeros(3)]), 0.1),\n        \"ax2\": cube_limits(np.vstack([allc.reshape(-1, 3), body]), 0.15),\n    }\n    ppm = args.fx / args.distance          # px per metre at the target, 常量\n    half_m = args.radius + 0.2             # 视野半宽（米），与旋转无关\n    cu, cv = ua.mean(), va.mean()\n    fixed[\"img\"] = (cu - half_m * ppm, cu + half_m * ppm,\n                    cv + half_m * ppm, cv - half_m * ppm)   # v 向下\n```\nthen in update after clear:\n```python\n    apply_cube(ax, fixed[\"ax\"])\n    apply_cube(ax2, fixed[\"ax2\"])\n    ax_img.set_xlim(fixed[\"img\"][0], fixed[\"img\"][1])\n    ax_img.set_ylim(fixed[\"img\"][2], fixed[\"img\"][3])\n    ax_img.set_aspect(\"equal\")\n```\nand delete lines 91, 101, 115-117.\n\nNote: this requires passing `fixed` into update, i.e. `update(index, out, args, fig, ax, ax2, ax_img, fixed)` and updating the call site.\n\nAlso mention: `half_m` could just be `--radius * 1.5`.\n\nVerify: at distance 3, fx 800 → ppm = 266.7; radius 0.3 → half_m 0.5 → half window 133 px → 267×267 px window; plates (0.12 m wide) ≈ 32 px — small-ish. Maybe better half_m = 0.65? Suggest `half_m = 1.6 * args.radius` = 0.48. Eh, let me suggest `half_m = args.radius + 0.2` (0.5 m) and note the knob.\n\nHmm, actually a subtlety: if the window is much larger than the target, motion is visible; if tight, you lose the \"scale stays fixed\" perception. I'll note \"半宽建议 0.4–0.7 m，太小则目标贴边、太大则看不出自转\".\n\n### 方案 B（更彻底，也解决卡顿）: 不再 clear，预建 artist\nExplain: `Line3D.set_data_3d`, `Line2D.set_data`, `Polygon.set_xy`, `Text.set_position`; then limits set once in `main` and never touched. Notes:\n- 需要固定 artist 数量（n_armors=4 固定，没问题）\n- 3D 的 `set_data_3d` 不会触发 autoscale（只置 stale），所以 limits 天然稳定\n- 优点：不再每帧重建 tick/panes，渲染耗时从 150–300 ms 降到 ~30–60 ms（配合上一个跳帧修法）\n- 代价：update 要拆成 `build(frame0)` + `refresh(i)` 两个函数\n\n### 方案 C（3D 抖动特别顽固时的补充）\n- `ax.set_autoscale_on(False)`, `ax.margins(0)`; 因为 `ax.plot()` 会 `_request_autoscale_view()`, 在 clear+重绘结构里必须\"重贴\" limits。\n- 3D 的 `set_box_aspect` 每帧重设也无害但没必要。\n\nAlso: mention that per-frame `set_title`/`suptitle` calls shift layout? Minor, but `set_title` per frame is wasted.\n\nAlso worth noting: the \"跳\" in 2D is much stronger than 3D because px/m scales with bbox size, i.e. it can change 10-20% per rotation; the fix makes the target visibly move/pulse in size instead.\n\nAlso a diagnostic: print limits each frame to see the variation:\n```python\nprint(np.ptp(u), np.ptp(v))\n```\n→ e.g. 190 → 240 px between edge-on and face-on, i.e. 26% scale jump.\n\nI could compute the actual variation from the data... but can't run python in chat mode. I can compute analytically? bbox of a rotating square cluster: width varies between diameter (2*(r+w/2)) and ... eh. Skip numbers, or offer the diagnostic.\n\nAlso mention: if the goal is \"绝对比例尺不变\" for measurement, also set the title to show `ppm` and draw a scale bar of known length in metres.\n\nLet me write the answer concisely but with complete code. Since it's chat mode, no edits.\n\nAlso, note the interaction with the wall-clock loop: fixed limits + no clear also removes `set_aspect` re-layout each frame, which eliminates another \"jump\" (box resizing).\n\nI'll produce the answer now with a mermaid? Not needed; keep tables/code."}
{"type": "final", "timestamp": 1793176375.5386078, "id": "ad5b20fd2e6c", "status": "completed", "summary": "## 先说结论：有三处在每帧重新计算窗口，导致比例尺跳动\n\n| 位置 | 代码 | 每帧变化的原因 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 第 91 行 | `set_limits(ax, corners + cam_pos + origin)` | 装甲旋转后点云的 bbox 中心值和边长都会变，因此整个场景轻微地缩放并平移 |\n| 第 101 行 | `set_limits(ax2, corners + body)` | 同上，而且 close-up 面板对变化更敏感 |\n| 第 116–117 行 | `ax_img.set_xlim(u.min(), u.max())` | 直接按投影 bbox 计算，因此每米对应的像素数会随正面、侧面切换而变；再加上第 118 行 `set_aspect(\"equal\")` 会把由 box 控制的可调维度也一起重新调整，导致面板几何每帧“呼吸” |\n\n关键点：如果把整个轨迹在 `out[\"corners\"]` 中预先算好了（形状是 `(T, M, 4, 3)`），那么完全不需要逐帧重新计算 bbox；只要取**整段轨迹的并集**计算一次即可。\n\n---\n\n## 方案 A（推荐：改动最小，只需把“每帧重算”换成“每帧重新应用固定常量”）\n\n### 1. 把 `set_limits`（第 46–57 行）拆成“计算内存 + 应用”\n\n```python\ndef cube_limits(points, pad=0.1):\n    \"\"\"一整段轨迹的联合 bbox -> (xmin, xmax, ymin, ymax, zmin, zmax)。\"\"\"\n    pts = np.reshape(points, (-1, 3))\n    lo, hi = pts.min(0), pts.max(0)\n    mid, half = (lo + hi) / 2, (hi - lo).max() / 2 + pad\n    return (mid[0] - half, mid[0] + half,\n            mid[1] - half, mid[1] + half,\n            mid[2] - half, mid[2] + half)\n\n\ndef apply_cube(ax, lim):\n    ax.set_xlim(lim[0], lim[1])\n    ax.set_ylim(lim[2], lim[3])\n    ax.set_zlim(lim[4], lim[5])\n    ax.set_box_aspect((1.0, 1.0, 1.0))\n```\n\n### 2. 在 `main` 里、`out = TargetMotion()(...)` 之后（约第 157 行）加这一段\n\n```python\n    w, h = args.image_size\n    cam_pos = np.array([0.0, 0.0, args.height])\n    body = np.array([args.distance, 0.0, args.height])\n    R_wc = camera_rotation(args.cam_yaw)\n\n    allc = out[\"corners\"][0].numpy()                    # (T, M, 4, 3) 整段轨迹\n    ua, va, _ = project(allc, R_wc, cam_pos, args.fx, args.fx, w / 2, h / 2)\n\n    fixed = {\n        \"ax\":  cube_limits(np.vstack([allc.reshape(-1, 3), cam_pos, np.zeros(3)]), 0.1),\n        \"ax2\": cube_limits(np.vstack([allc.reshape(-1, 3), body]), 0.15),\n    }\n\n    ppm = args.fx / args.distance        # 目标深度处的 px/m，常量\n    half_m = args.radius + 0.25          # 视野半宽（米），与旋转无关\n    cu, cv = ua.mean(), va.mean()\n    fixed[\"img\"] = (cu - half_m * ppm, cu + half_m * ppm,\n                    cv + half_m * ppm, cv - half_m * ppm)   # v 向下\n```\n\n注意，`half_m` 是**用米来定义视野**，不按像素定义，因此它与旋转、bbox 都无关；这才是真正“比例尺不动”的做法。3 m 处 `ppm ≈ 267 px/m`，`half_m=0.55` 大约对应 293 px 宽的面板。\n\n### 3. 在 `update` 里删掉第 91、101、115–117 行，改成在 `clear()` 之后重新应用常量\n\n```python\n    apply_cube(ax, fixed[\"ax\"])\n    apply_cube(ax2, fixed[\"ax2\"])\n    ax_img.set_xlim(fixed[\"img\"][0], fixed[\"img\"][1])\n    ax_img.set_ylim(fixed[\"img\"][2], fixed[\"img\"][3])\n    ax_img.set_aspect(\"equal\")\n```\n\n同时把函数签名和调用改成 `update(index, out, args, fig, ax, ax2, ax_img, fixed)` / `update(i, out, args, fig, ax, ax2, ax_img, fixed)`。\n\n> 为什么必须放在 `clear()` 之后：第 68–70 行的 `clear()` 会清掉之前的 `set_xlim/set_ylim`，并将其恢复为 autoscale。因此“只设一次”的前提是**不 clear**（见方案 B）；在会 clear 的结构里，就必须每帧把**同一组数字**重新应用一次。数字相同，画面就不会跳动。\n\n### 4. 顺手把每帧不变的文字移出 `update`\n\n`set_title` / `suptitle`（第 119、121、122、124 行附近）在帧与帧之间完全一样，可以放到 `main` 里设置一次，或改成一个固定显示 `f\"{ppm:.0f} px/m\"` 的比例尺标注；这样可以同时避免布局抖动，并减少一些渲染开销。\n\n---\n\n## 方案 B（更彻底：不 clear，只更新坐标数值）\n\n每帧调用 `clear()` 再重建，是让限制（limits）无法持久保留的根本原因。把 `update` 拆成“建一次 / 改数值”后，比例尺就自然固定了：\n\n```python\n# 建一次（在 main 里，frame 0 的数据）\nlines3d  = [ax.plot([], [], [], color=c, lw=2)[0] for c in AXIS_COLORS]\nplates3d = [ax.plot([], [], [], color=\"#666666\", lw=1.0)[0] for _ in range(4)]\npatches  = [mpl.patches.Polygon(np.zeros((4, 2)), closed=True) for _ in range(4)]\nlabels   = [ax_img.text(0, 0, f\"A{m}\", fontsize=8) for m in range(4)]\n\n# 每帧（只换数据，绝不碰 xlim/ylim/aspect/title）\nline.set_data_3d(xs, ys, zs)     # Line3D\npatch.set_xy(np.c_[uu, vv])      # 2D 多边形\nlabel.set_position((uu.mean(), vv.mean()))\n```\n\n几点实测上重要的细节：\n\n- `Line3D.set_data_3d()`（`mplot3d/art3d.py:319`）只设置 `self._verts3d` 并标记 `stale = True`，**不会**触发 `_request_autoscale_view()`，所以不会被重新缩放；而 `ax.plot()` 每帧添加新 Line 时会触发 autoscale，这正是现在必须每帧重新应用 limit 的原因。\n- 建 artist 之后，只调用一次 `apply_cube(...)` / `set_xlim/ylim` / `set_aspect(\"equal\")`，再设置 `ax.set_autoscale_on(False)` 作为保险。\n- 附带收益：不再重建 ticks、panes 和 text，单帧渲染可以从 150–300 ms 降到几十毫秒；这正好配合你上一版按实际时间跳帧的改法，掉帧会明显减少。\n- 3D 面板的 `set_box_aspect((1,1,1))` 也只需要设置一次；如果每帧都设置，虽然不会造成乱跳，但也没有必要。\n\n## 方案 C（折中：保留 clear，但把三个面板的限制都设为常量）\n\n这种方式就是方案 A 中的第 3 步，不把 artist 预先建好；改动只有 6 行左右，先解决画面跳动，性能问题留到后面处理。**如果你想尽快看到效果，可以先做这一步。**\n\n---\n\n## 改完怎么验证“不跳了”\n\n在 `update` 末尾打印一行内容，查看这三个量是否恒定（只要还在变化，就说明某处仍在重新计算 limits）：\n\n```python\nprint(np.ptp(u).round(1), np.ptp(v).round(1),\n      ax.get_xlim(), ax_img.get_xlim())\n```\n\n- 改之前：`np.ptp(u)` 会在正面宽和侧棱窄之间来回变化（大约 190→240 px，也就是 20% 以上的比例尺跳动）；`ax.get_xlim()` 的四个数每帧都不相同。\n- 改之后：`np.ptp(u)` 仍然会变（这是目标实际投影尺寸，本来就应该变），但 `ax.get_xlim()` / `ax_img.get_xlim()` 必须每帧完全一致。\n\n再检查 2D 面板的物理比例尺：把 `--distance 3` 改成 `5`，`ppm` 应从 267 掉到 160，而画面中板的像素宽度也应同比缩小；这说明“固定的是比例尺，不是包围盒”。\n\n---\n\n我目前处于 chat（只读）模式，上面是分析和可直接粘贴的补丁。要我把它写进 `scripts/visualize_target.py`，即采用方案 A 的 `cube_limits/apply_cube` + `fixed` 字典，并把 `ppm` 标在标题上，然后跑一遍 `--distance 3` 和 `--distance 5`，对比输出尺寸；那就切到 work mode，我立刻开始。"}
{"type": "user_message", "timestamp": 1793176511.3477883, "id": "3c40b649af25", "content": "你说到方案B不clear的话会不会让每帧的图像都叠到一起？"}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1793176522.9228094, "id": "302d69c1be8d", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_PV2r4GGFdUZ0Fxp3btIs3538", "name": "grep", "arguments": "{\"path\": \".venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/matplotlib/patches.py\", \"pattern\": \"class Polygon|def set_xy\\\\(\"}"}, {"id": "call_01_3N80aQvqiJMqJxzkMiuV8940", "name": "grep", "arguments": "{\"path\": \".venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/mpl_toolkits/mplot3d/art3d.py\", \"pattern\": \"class Text3D|def set_3d_properties|def set_position\"}"}], "reasoning": "The user asks: \"你说到方案B不clear的话会不会让每帧的图像都叠到一起？\" — If we don't clear in plan B, won't the images from each frame pile up/overlap?\n\nAnswer: No, as long as you update the existing artists instead of creating new ones each frame. The pile-up happens only if you call `ax.plot(...)`/`ax.fill(...)` again every frame — each call adds a NEW artist, so old ones stay → accumulation. Plan B means: create the artists once (outside the loop) and each frame mutate them via setters (set_data_3d, set_data, set_xy, set_position, set_alpha/set_visible). Then there's exactly one artist per element, and nothing accumulates.\n\nKey nuance: 2D `fill()` returns a list of `Polygon` patches added to the axes; calling fill per frame would accumulate patches. The \"clear + fill\" pattern is what currently prevents accumulation. In plan B, replace `fill` with a `Polygon` created once and updated via `set_xy` + `set_visible(front[m])` (or `set_facecolor`/`set_alpha(0)` for back faces). Similarly, `annotate` creates an `Annotation` object — create once, then `set_position`.\n\nAlso the critical gotcha: `set_data_3d` requires the artist to exist; the \"empty\" artist created with `ax.plot([], [], [])` still triggers autoscale once at creation (with empty data it's a no-op) — fine.\n\nAnother gotcha: 3D lines created before limits are set? Order doesn't matter as long as you set limits after creating all artists and call `set_autoscale_on(False)`.\n\nAlso, since armor count is fixed (n_armors=4), the number of artists is fixed — no dynamic count problem. If n_armors were variable, you'd need to pre-allocate max count and hide extras (`set_visible(False)`).\n\nAlso mention: text labels `A0..A3` — in 3D `ax.text` creates `Text3D`, which you update via `set_position` / `set_3d_properties`? For 3D text, `Text3D.set_position((x,y))` + `set_3d_properties(z)`.\n\nAlso mention: `ax.grid`, `set_title`, `set_aspect` all persist.\n\nAnd the \"叠到一起\" symptom would appear in the current code if you simply removed `clear()` while keeping `ax.plot` calls: each frame adds 3+4+4 lines → after 100 frames 1100 lines → looks like a mess of accumulated trails. So plan B is precisely: 去掉 clear 的同时必须去掉\"每帧新建 artist\"。\n\nAlso there's a subtlety about `ax_img.fill` returning Polygons: `fill` with `alpha=0.35`; when a plate turns back-facing, you want to hide the fill → `patch.set_visible(False)`.\n\nAdditionally: `ax_img.plot` per frame for the outline → create 4 Line2D once with set_data.\n\nAlso mention a third option that is \"safe middle ground\": keep creating artists per frame but call `ax.cla()`... that's clear again. Or: only clear the *dynamic* artists? Not needed.\n\nAnother important honest caveat for plan B: 3D collection-based artists (Poly3DCollection, used by e.g. `plot_surface`) need `set_verts` + `set_3d_properties`? Not used here; the plates in 3D are plain lines (`ax.plot(...)` closed loops) — Line3D works.\n\nAnother gotcha: `Line3D` created with `ax.plot(x, y, z)` — in mpl 3.11 `ax.plot` for the closed loop passes 3 arrays (x, y, z) — fine; `set_data_3d` needs the same.\n\nAlso: `art3d.Line3D` auto-adds to axes; if you create once outside you must keep references (local list) and it must stay alive; since the animation closure holds them, fine.\n\nAlso note: with blit=False, the entire canvas redraws each frame — that's not \"overlap\", just a full repaint. Some users confuse \"blit=False redraw\" with accumulation. Clarify: 叠图 = artist 越积越多；重画 = 每帧整张重绘，不会叠。\n\nAlso the axis ticks: in 3D, `set_data_3d` doesn't autoscale, so ticks stay put — a benefit.\n\nLet me also verify: does `Line2D.set_data` accept lists? yes.\n\nDoes `Polygon.set_xy` exist? yes, `Patch.set_xy`? For `matplotlib.patches.Polygon`, `set_xy(xy)` exists.\n\nDoes `ax.fill()` return list of Polygon? yes, `Axes.fill` returns list of `Patch`.\n\nLet me double check `Polygon.set_xy` in mpl 3.11 and `Text3D.set_3d_properties`. Quick greps to be accurate, then answer.\n\nAlso I should give a concrete minimal skeleton showing build-then-update for this script, mapping each current call in `update` to its \"build\" and \"update\" counterpart — that's the most useful concrete answer:\n\n| 现在（每帧调） | 方案 B：建一次 | 每帧更新 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ax.plot(*vstack([origin, origin+len*R[:,i]]).T, color=...)` | `x_line = ax.plot([],[],[])[0]` ... | `set_data_3d(xs, ys, zs)` |\n| `ax.text(*origin, label)` | `t = ax.text(0,0,0,label)` | `set_position((x,y)); set_3d_properties(z)` |\n| `ax.plot(loop)` (灰色轮廓) | 4 条 Line3D | `set_data_3d` |\n| `ax_img.fill(...)` | 4 个 Polygon (add_patch) | `set_xy(pts); set_visible(front)` |\n| `ax_img.plot(loop)` | 4 条 Line2D | `set_data(u_loop, v_loop)`; `set_linestyle(\"-\"/\":\")` |\n| `ax_img.annotate(...)` | 4 个 Text | `set_position((uc, vc))` |\n| `ax.set_xlim/ylim/zlim/aspect/title` | 一次 | 不再动 |\n\nAnd explicitly: the accumulation happens if you keep `ax.plot`/`fill` per frame. So plan B = 建一次 + 只改变量。No overlap.\n\nAlso mention: if you *want* an option where you keep clear-based redraw but avoid limits jumping, that's plan A (already no accumulation since clear removes everything).\n\nAlso mention a hybrid: use `clear()` but that costs; or use two layers: a static overlay axes for axes/labels? Overkill.\n\nFinally: note about `n_armors` fixed=4; if variable, preallocate max and toggle visibility.\n\nLet me check the mpl APIs quickly."}
