{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1793176705.5284317, "id": "f24d84807686", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_U5vu3yhUhvo1H7xUChWn9490", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd /home/fanshu/Workspace/qianli_auto_aim_simulation && cat > /tmp/ascii3.py <<\\\"PYEOF\\\"\\nimport numpy as np\\nfrom PIL import Image\\na = np.asarray(Image.open(\\\"/tmp/vis_check.png\\\").convert(\\\"RGB\\\")).astype(int)\\nh, w, _ = a.shape\\np = a[:, 2 * w // 3:]\\nH, W = p.shape[:2]\\ncols, rows = 70, 26\\nchars = \\\" .:-=+*#%@\\\"\\nfor r in range(rows):\\n    line = \\\"\\\"\\n    for c in range(cols):\\n        blk = p[r * H // rows:(r + 1) * H // rows, c * W // cols:(c + 1) * W // cols]\\n        ink = (blk < 250).any(-1).mean()\\n        line += chars[min(len(chars) - 1, int(ink * len(chars) * 2))]\\n    print(line)\\nPYEOF\\n.venv/bin/python /tmp/ascii3.py\"}"}, {"id": "call_01_1DPlTwOgq0QI15Uzre5k2744", "name": "run_command", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd /home/fanshu/Workspace/qianli_auto_aim_simulation && .venv/bin/python -c \\\"\\nimport sys; sys.argv=['x']\\nimport scripts.visualize_target as v\\ntry:\\n    v.main(['--duration','0'])\\nexcept SystemExit as e:\\n    print('duration 0 ->', e)\\ntry:\\n    v.main(['--fps','-1'])\\nexcept SystemExit as e:\\n    print('fps -1 ->', e)\\n\\\"\"}"}], "reasoning": "Per-frame full redraw at dpi 100 = ~98 ms → ~10 fps ceiling. The wall-clock skipping handles it (motion stays real-time), but frames drop to ~10/s. With dpi 80 it might be ~60ms. The 3D axes dominate.\n\nCan we speed up? Options:\n- The `blit=False` full-figure draw is the cost; artists update is cheap. Matplotlib 3D can't blit. We could reduce dpi to 80 → maybe 60 ms.\n- Could set `ax.set_proj_type` etc. no.\n\nSince the user cares about smoothness maybe, but main ask is fixed scale. Report measured ~98 ms/frame (≈10 fps ceiling at default dpi 100), so with default fps 60 the wall-clock loop will drop frames but keep real time. They can lower `--dpi` for smoother playback.\n\nLet me measure dpi 80 quickly to give a recommendation. Also check that the \"empty artists\" don't add cost.\n\nAlso verify the ASCII/visual sanity of /tmp/vis_check.png: panel 3 ink is only 9618 px of 1320/3*416 ≈ 183k — plates are small in a big window. At 3 m, plate cluster ~160 px wide inside a 294 px window — but ink 9618 suggests small. Let's estimate: 4 plates 32×16 px each ≈ 2000 px area, outlines ~ 4*2*(32+16) ≈ 400... fill alpha maybe counted (<250). Hmm 9618 includes annotate text. Plausible.\n\nMaybe increase the default window tightness so panel 3 reads better: half = (radius+0.25)*ppm = 147 px at 3 m; window 294×294. The cluster is 160 px wide → occupies 54% width. That's reasonable.\n\nLet me eyeball via a coarse ASCII of panel 3 to ensure plates are visible and centered. Convert to ASCII with 60 cols.\n\nAlso let me check the first frame's title/labels and that panel 1 & 2 have visible axes.\n\nThen final: also verify invalid args error, and run with `--dpi 80` timing.\n\nAlso confirm no leftover references to removed things (e.g., `--out` removed; `label_axes` used).\n\nLet me do ASCII check + arg error + dpi timing."}
