hs` only used for iteration count; slight redundancy but readable.\n\nPotential issue: unused variable `a0` in test only.\n\nLet's read the final file sections to double check nothing is off (e.g., duplicate lines from the write).\n\nAlso: `for a in (ax, ax2): label_axes(a)`.\n\nRead file lines 100-180 to confirm.\n\nThen save memory and summarize.\n\nActually, one more improvement worth considering: since `set_autoscale_on(False)` is set on ax_img, and `set_aspect(\"equal\")` with `adjustable=\"box\"` — stable. ✓.\n\nAlso: with autoscale off, if the user passes `--radius` bigger, `fixed[\"ax\"]` computed from trajectory → fine.\n\nAlso: `--image-size` affects the window center/px scale (uses w/2,h/2) ✓.\n\nLet me review the final file quickly."}
