{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1793177915.7092648, "id": "9f393f94d33b", "tool_call_id": "call_00_zYyYYNH8WyRCJiR7zV6j7601", "content": "OK: command succeeded\nstdout:\n475:    def draw(self, renderer):\n    def draw(self, renderer):\n        if not self.get_visible():\n            return\n        self._unstale_viewLim()\n\n        # draw the background patch\n        self.patch.draw(renderer)\n        self._frameon = False\n\n        # first, set the aspect\n        # this is duplicated from `axes._base._AxesBase.draw`\n        # but must be called before any of the artist are drawn as\n        # it adjusts the view limits and the size of the bounding box\n        # of the Axes\n        locator = self.get_axes_locator()\n        self.apply_aspect(locator(self, renderer) if locator else None)\n\n        # add the projection matrix to the axes\n        self.M = self.get_proj()\n        self.invM = np.linalg.inv(self.M)\n\n        collections_and_patches = (\n            artist for artist in self._children\n            if isinstance(artist, (mcoll.Collection, mpatches.Patch))\n            and artist.get_visible())\n        if self.computed_zorder:\n            # Calculate projection of collections and patches and zorder\n            # them. Make sure they are drawn above the grids.\n            zorder_offset = max(axis.get_zorder()\n                                for axis in self._axis_map.values()) + 1\n            collection_zorder = patch_zorder = zorder_offset\n\n            for artist in sorted(collections_and_patches,\n                                 key=lambda artist: artist.do_3d_projection(),\n                                 reverse=True):\n                if isinstance(artist, mcoll.Collection):\n                    artist.zorder = collection_zorder\n                    collection_zorder += 1\n                elif isinstance(artist, mpatches.Patch):\n                    artist.zorder = patch_zorder\n                    patch_zorder += 1\n        else:\n            for artist in collections_and_patches:\n                artist.do_3d_projection()\n\n        if self._axis3don:\n            # Draw panes first\n            for axis in self._axis_map.values():\n                axis.draw_pane(renderer)\n            # Then gridlines\n            for axis in self._axis_map.values():\n                axis.draw_grid(renderer)\n            # Then axes, labels, text, and ticks\n            for axis in self._axis_map.values():\n                axis.draw(renderer)\n\n        # Then rest\n        super().draw(renderer)\n\n    def get_axis_position(self):\n", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1793177936.4339485, "id": "68846103a094", "content": "## 结论先说\n\n`update()` 本身的开销可以忽略：每帧只是对 4×4 个点的 numpy 计算，耗时不到 1 ms。之前的实测已经表明，整幅重绘约 **94 ms**，并且把 `dpi` 改成 60/80/100 时耗时几乎不变（92–98 ms），这说明瓶颈在于 **artist/pane 的绘制开销，而不在像素填充**。因此只有减少每帧要绘制的对象数量，或者干脆不进行全幅重绘，才能继续降低延迟。\n\n## 94 ms 花在哪里（依据 mpl 源码）\n\n`Axes3D.draw()`（`mplot3d/axes3d.py:475`）每帧固定执行以下工作：\n\n| 阶段 | 每帧动作 | 我们的量 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 投影矩阵 | `self.M = self.get_proj()` + `np.linalg.inv(M)` ×2 面板 | 便宜 |\n| collection/patch 排序 | 对每个可绘制对象调用 `do_3d_projection()` 后排序 | 各 3 pane |\n| `_axis3don` 分支 | 每个轴 `draw_pane()` → `draw_grid()` → `draw()`（轴线+刻度+**刻度文本**+offset text） | 2 面板 × 3 轴 |\n| `super().draw()` | 我们的 artist：13 + 19 条 Line3D + 标签 | — |\n| `ax_image.draw` | 4 Polygon + 4 Line2D + 4 Text + 网格 | 便宜 |\n\n`set_axis_off()` 直接把 `_axis3don` 设为 `False`（`axes3d.py:220`），于是 `axis3d.py:520` 的整个绘制块都会被跳过——**pane 的 alpha 多边形、网格集合、约 20 个刻度文本会全部消失**。这就是最大的开销来源；而 3D 线本身只占一小部分。\n\n## 四档方案（按收益/风险排序）\n\n| 方案 | 改法 | 预期每帧 | 代价 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **① blit** | `FuncAnimation(..., blit=True)` + `animate()` 返回 artist 列表 | **~5–15 ms**（约 5–10×） | 3D 视图不能再交互旋转（鼠标拖拽会触发后台重绘，mpl 会重建背景，可接受） |\n| **② 关掉 3D 轴装饰** | `ax_world.set_axis_off()`、`ax_armor.set_axis_off()` | ~30–45 ms（约 2–3×） | 没有 pane/网格/刻度，失去读数参考（轴标签也会消失，可改用 `fig.text` 说明） |\n| **③ 3D 面板改手算正交投影的 2D 轴** | 两个 3D 面板用 numpy 投到 2D，用普通 `Line2D` 画 | ~15–25 ms（约 4–6×） | 去掉 `Axes3D` 本身（不再有鼠标旋转），但轴架本来就由我们自己画，视觉几乎不变 |\n| **④ 少一个面板 / `antialiased=False`** | 删掉装甲特写面板；线宽抗锯齿关掉 | −40% / −5–10% | 信息量减少 / 线条略毛糙 |\n\n**推荐组合：①，必要时叠加 ②**。② 与 ①（blit）可叠加使用：blit 只重画变化对象，`set_axis_off` 省掉一次性的后台开销。\n\n## 方案①的具体改法（4 行）\n\n现在 `animate()` 只 `update(index)`、不返回 artist，所以先登记“会动的 artist”：所有对象都只建一次，列表可以直接拼：\n\n```python\nmoving = ([a for lines, text, _ in world_frames + armor_frames\n           for a in (*lines, text)]\n          + world_plates + armor_plates + fills + edges + tags)\n\ndef animate(_tick):\n    index = min(int((time.perf_counter() - start) / SECONDS * N_FRAMES),\n                N_FRAMES - 1)\n    update(index)\n    if index == N_FRAMES - 1:\n        animation.event_source.stop()\n    return moving                       # blit 只重画这些\n\nanimation = FuncAnimation(fig, animate, interval=1000.0 / FPS, repeat=False,\n                          blit=True, cache_frame_data=False)\n```\n\n3D 能 blit 的前提正好我们已经满足：`Line3D.draw` / `Text3D.do_3d_projection` 用 `self.axes.M`，而这个矩阵在后台那次完整 `Axes3D.draw()` 里已经算好；只要**视角和 limits 不变**（我们正是整段定死的），blit 后的帧就是正确的。若某个后端（个别 Qt/Wayland 组合）出现残影，把 `blit=True` 去掉即可回退。\n\n## 方案③的思路（若想彻底摆脱 `Axes3D`）\n\n投影只需要 6 行，和你已有的 `project()` 同构：\n\n```python\ndef ortho(points, elev=25.0, azim=-60.0):\n    \"\"\"3D points -> 2D screen coords + depth (orthographic, like Axes3D).\"\"\"\n    e, a = np.radians(elev), np.radians(azim)\n    right = np.array([-np.sin(a), np.cos(a), 0.0])\n    up = np.array([-np.sin(e) * np.cos(a), -np.sin(e) * np.sin(a), np.cos(e)])\n    return points @ right, points @ up, points @ np.cross(right, up)\n```\n\n之后每个面板就是普通 2D `Axes` + `Line2D.set_data()`，每帧 36 条短折线，Agg 绘制成本远低于 `Axes3D`。\n\n## 顺手可做的小项（收益小但免费）\n\n- `interval` 从 `1000/FPS`（16.7 ms）改成按实测帧时间（如 `1000/15` ≈ 67 ms），不再请求渲染不出来的帧。\n- 线的 `lw` 保持 ≥1、`antialiased=False` 可省几个百分点。\n- **不要**再去调 `figsize`/`dpi`——已实测无效（92–98 ms 不变）。\n\n## 验证方法（改完直接量）\n\n```python\nt0 = time.perf_counter(); fig.canvas.draw()\nprint(round((time.perf_counter() - t0) * 1e3, 1), \"ms\")\n```\n\n分别测：`fig.canvas.draw()`（基线 94 ms）、`ax_world.draw(renderer)` / `ax_armor.draw(renderer)` / `ax_image.draw(renderer)`（看两面板各占多少）、`update(i)`（确认 <1 ms）；再测 `set_axis_off()` 与 `grid(False)+pane.set_visible(False)` 变体做对比——这样就能直接看出哪个方案真正有效，不必只凭猜测。\n\n—\n\n要我把 ①（blit）实测并改进去吗？现在处于 chat 模式，只能读不能写，也跑不了 `.venv/bin/python`；切到 work 模式（Run 旁边的按钮）我就按上面顺序做，先量出 94 ms 的分解，再给你改后的每帧耗时对比。", "tool_calls": [], "reasoning": "This confirms the per-frame work:\n- `self.M = self.get_proj()`, `invM = np.linalg.inv(self.M)` (cheap)\n- for every collection/patch: `do_3d_projection()` (sorting) — our panels have panes as Patch3D → 3 per axis × ... plus gridlines as Line3DCollection\n- if `_axis3don`: per axis: `draw_pane` (alpha polygon over the axes area), `draw_grid` (a Line3DCollection with many segments), `draw` (axis line, ticks, tick labels, offset text)\n- then `super().draw()` draws all children: our Line3D artists + Text3D.\n\nKey cost centers: 3 panes per axes (alpha-blended big polygons), 3 grid collections (each with ~6-7 line segments but as a collection → path conversion each frame), ticks+labels (Agg text ~0.05-0.3 ms each), plus per-artist draw of ~19 lines.\n\nSo `set_axis_off()` kills pane+grid+ticks+labels for that axes → the majority.\n\nI can strengthen the answer with the counts of artists/text on our axes: from earlier checks — `ax_world.lines` 13, `ax_armor.lines` 19. Plus panes/grid/ticks.\n\nMaybe I can measure the *static* composition cheaply? Can't run python. So I'll present estimates as estimates, clearly labeled, and give the ordering rationale based on the draw() code above.\n\nI could still gather some read-only evidence about how many ticks/labels are drawn: with fixed cube limits spanning e.g. 3.7 m, default AutoLocator gives ~5-7 ticks per axis → ~18-21 tick labels + 3 axis labels per 3D axes. Grid collections: 3 per axes (one per axis direction) each with 5-7 segments, drawn as Line3DCollection → each draw does path transform + segment rendering.\n\nAlso note: Text rendering in Agg is the single most expensive artist type per unit area; ~1-3 ms per 100 glyphs? Honestly, a rough per-label cost is 0.05–0.2 ms at 10 pt.\n\nTotal: 2 panels × (3 panes + 3 grids + ~20 tick labels + 3 axis labels + ~16 lines) ≈ plausible 35-45 ms per panel.\n\nNow, the answer: present the diagnosis, four optimization options with expected savings and risk, plus recommended combination, plus the concrete patch for the best one (blit), and offer to implement in work mode with before/after numbers.\n\nLet me write the blit patch concretely for the current