{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1793178088.2721775, "id": "41583ceaf293", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_v4i33NUYsrfJEUUd96tU7912", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"content\": \"import os, sys, runpy\\nimport matplotlib\\nmatplotlib.use(\\\"Agg\\\")\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\nimport matplotlib.animation as manim\\n\\nsys.path.insert(0, os.getcwd())\\nplt.show = lambda *a, **k: None\\nmanim.FuncAnimation = type(\\\"Cap\\\", (manim.FuncAnimation,), {})\\n\\ng = runpy.run_path(\\\"scripts/visualize_target.py\\\", run_name=\\\"__main__\\\")\\nfig, update, n = g[\\\"fig\\\"], g[\\\"update\\\"], g[\\\"N_FRAMES\\\"]\\nmoving, axw, axa, axi = g[\\\"moving\\\"], g[\\\"ax_world\\\"], g[\\\"ax_armor\\\"], g[\\\"ax_image\\\"]\\n\\n\\ndef buf():\\n    return np.asarray(fig.canvas.buffer_rgba())[..., :3].astype(int)\\n\\n\\nupdate(0)\\nfig.canvas.draw()\\nbg = fig.canvas.copy_from_bbox(fig.bbox)\\n\\ni = 200\\nupdate(i)\\nfig.canvas.draw()\\nfull = buf()\\nfig.canvas.restore_region(bg)\\nfor a in moving:\\n    a.axes.draw_artist(a)\\nfig.canvas.blit(fig.bbox)\\nblitted = buf()\\nmask = np.abs(blitted - full).max(-1) > 8\\nys, xs = np.nonzero(mask)\\nprint(\\\"differing pixels:\\\", mask.sum())\\nprint(\\\"bbox rows %d..%d  cols %d..%d  (image %dx%d)\\\"\\n      % (ys.min(), ys.max(), xs.min(), xs.max(), full.shape[1], full.shape[0]))\\nfor name, ax in ((\\\"world\\\", axw), (\\\"armor\\\", axa), (\\\"image\\\", axi)):\\n    bb = ax.get_window_extent().padded(10)\\n    h = full.shape[0]\\n    lo_y, hi_y = int(h - bb.y1), int(h - bb.y0)\\n    sub = mask[max(lo_y, 0):hi_y, max(int(bb.x0), 0):int(bb.x1)]\\n    print(\\\"  %-6s window rows %d..%d cols %d..%d -> %d diff px\\\"\\n          % (name, lo_y, hi_y, int(bb.x0), int(bb.x1), sub.sum()))\\n\\n# where are the texts in the world panel?\\nfor t in axw.texts:\\n    d = t.get_window_extent()\\n    h = full.shape[0]\\n    sub = mask[int(h - d.y1) - 2:int(h - d.y0) + 2, int(d.x0) - 2:int(d.x1) + 2]\\n    print(\\\"  text %-2s at %4.0f,%4.0f size %2.0fx%2.0f -> %d diff px\\\"\\n          % (t.get_text(), d.x0, h - d.y0, d.width, d.height, sub.sum()))\\nfor t in axi.texts:\\n    d = t.get_window_extent()\\n    h = full.shape[0]\\n    sub = mask[int(h - d.y1) - 2:int(h - d.y0) + 2, int(d.x0) - 2:int(d.x1) + 2]\\n    print(\\\"  tag  %-3s size %2.0fx%2.0f -> %d diff px\\\" % (t.get_text(), d.width, d.height, sub.sum()))\\n\", \"path\": \"/tmp/check_blit3.py\"}"}], "reasoning": "Interesting: full(i+1) vs full(i) differ 0.000% — meaning `update(i+1)` doesn't change the rendering?! That means... hmm, `update(i+1)` after `update(i)` — full draws are identical? That can't be right if the armor moves. Unless... `fig.canvas.draw()` after `restore_region`/`blit` didn't repaint? Wait: after a blit, the canvas buffer contains bg+artists; calling `fig.canvas.draw()` should redraw fully. Hmm.\n\nOh! The issue: `fig.canvas.draw()` — if all artists are `stale=False`, mpl may skip? No, full draw always redraws.\n\nWait, maybe the real problem: `update()` doesn't mark artists stale, so `fig.canvas.draw()` now *skips* drawing non-stale artists? In Agg, `FigureCanvasAgg.draw()` calls `self.figure.draw(renderer)` → `fig.draw()` → `Artist.draw` for children; `draw` executes regardless of stale (stale only affects `draw_idle` scheduling). Hmm, but `_draw_list_compositing_images` draws all children unconditionally.\n\nHmm, but `Line2D.draw` does `if not self.get_visible(): return` and also caches? In mpl 3.11, `Line2D.draw` has:\n```python\n    def draw(self, renderer):\n        # docstring inherited\n        if not self.get_visible():\n            return\n        if self._x is None or self._y is None:\n            return\n        if self._invalid:\n            self._transform_path()? \n```\nHmm, mpl 3.11 introduced `Artist.stale` caching for text/lines? Let me check `Line2D.draw` in mpl 3.11 — I believe there is `self._cached_...`? Actually in mpl 3.10 there's \"Line2D.draw\" using `self._linewidth`... no caching.\n\nBut wait: what about `Text.draw`? mpl 3.11 does cache text layout with `self._get_layout` and `self.stale`? Text caching exists (`_Text2D`?). Hmm.\n\nBigger clue: after `blit` and then `fig.canvas.draw()` the diff vs `full` is 0.000% for `full(i+1) vs full(i)` — this suggests the second `fig.canvas.draw()` didn't change anything, i.e. it was a no-op. Maybe because I called `fig.canvas.blit(...)`, and Agg's `blit` in this mode... no.\n\nHold on: maybe `fig.canvas.draw()` DID redraw, but `update(i+1)` produced identical geometry because... the plate geometry at i and i+1 is very similar but not identical — a 0.000% pixel diff with threshold >8 could still be possible? At 10 fps sampling of a spinning target, consecutive frames (1/60 s) move only ~0.3° → the projected plate shifts by <0.1 px → below the >8 threshold. Yes! Frame index 200 vs 201 differ by 1/60 s → negligible visual change. So 0.000% is plausible for adjacent frames. Bad control.\n\nSo the 0.52% diff between blit and full at the SAME index is real. Where? Max diff 255 (pure difference, black/white). It's the same 0.5% at all three indices, suggesting a systematic difference — likely something drawn in the full draw but not in blit (or vice versa): e.g. the *text labels* — Text3D draws with a `_setattr_cm` context; in the blit path, text is drawn... hmm, but we include texts.\n\nOr: the axes 2D panel's grid lines? They're background (not in moving) → present in both.\n\nLet me diff-visualize: find the bounding boxes of differing pixels, per panel. Likely they're around the text labels (font rasterization) — since Text3D in blit is drawn via `draw_artist` which sets clip box etc. and might render with a different antialiasing/position? Or the 2D `tags` text.\n\nLet me locate the diff region: compute mask, then report bounding boxes and count per third of the image. Also check whether differences occur exactly where the text labels are.\n\nAlternatively compare \"blit vs full\" for a *subset*: e.g. compare only the 2D panel region (x > 2/3 width) vs 3D regions.\n\nLet me analyze the diff mask."}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1793178088.2721071, "id": "02efbe66be43", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"content\": \"import os, sys, runpy\\nimport matplotlib\\nmatplotlib.use(\\\"Agg\\\")\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\nimport matplotlib.animation as manim\\n\\nsys.path.insert(0, os.getcwd())\\nplt.show = lambda *a, **k: None\\nmanim.FuncAnimation = type(\\\"Cap\\\", (manim.FuncAnimation,), {})\\n\\ng = runpy.run_path(\\\"scripts/visualize_target.py\\\", run_name=\\\"__main__\\\")\\nfig, update, n = g[\\\"fig\\\"], g[\\\"update\\\"], g[\\\"N_FRAMES\\\"]\\nmoving, axw, axa, axi = g[\\\"moving\\\"], g[\\\"ax_world\\\"], g[\\\"ax_armor\\\"], g[\\\"ax_image\\\"]\\n\\n\\ndef buf():\\n    return np.asarray(fig.canvas.buffer_rgba())[..., :3].astype(int)\\n\\n\\nupdate(0)\\nfig.canvas.draw()\\nbg = fig.canvas.copy_from_bbox(fig.bbox)\\n\\ni = 200\\nupdate(i)\\nfig.canvas.draw()\\nfull = buf()\\nfig.canvas.restore_region(bg)\\nfor a in moving:\\n    a.axes.draw_artist(a)\\nfig.canvas.blit(fig.bbox)\\nblitted = buf()\\nmask = np.abs(blitted - full).max(-1) > 8\\nys, xs = np.nonzero(mask)\\nprint(\\\"differing pixels:\\\", mask.sum())\\nprint(\\\"bbox rows %d..%d  cols %d..%d  (image %dx%d)\\\"\\n      % (ys.min(), ys.max(), xs.min(), xs.max(), full.shape[1], full.shape[0]))\\nfor name, ax in ((\\\"world\\\", axw), (\\\"armor\\\", axa), (\\\"image\\\", axi)):\\n    bb = ax.get_window_extent().padded(10)\\n    h = full.shape[0]\\n    lo_y, hi_y = int(h - bb.y1), int(h - bb.y0)\\n    sub = mask[max(lo_y, 0):hi_y, max(int(bb.x0), 0):int(bb.x1)]\\n    print(\\\"  %-6s window rows %d..%d cols %d..%d -> %d diff px\\\"\\n          % (name, lo_y, hi_y, int(bb.x0), int(bb.x1), sub.sum()))\\n\\n# where are the texts in the world panel?\\nfor t in axw.texts:\\n    d = t.get_window_extent()\\n    h = full.shape[0]\\n    sub = mask[int(h - d.y1) - 2:int(h - d.y0) + 2, int(d.x0) - 2:int(d.x1) + 2]\\n    print(\\\"  text %-2s at %4.0f,%4.0f size %2.0fx%2.0f -> %d diff px\\\"\\n          % (t.get_text(), d.x0, h - d.y0, d.width, d.height, sub.sum()))\\nfor t in axi.texts:\\n    d = t.get_window_extent()\\n    h = full.shape[0]\\n    sub = mask[int(h - d.y1) - 2:int(h - d.y0) + 2, int(d.x0) - 2:int(d.x1) + 2]\\n    print(\\\"  tag  %-3s size %2.0fx%2.0f -> %d diff px\\\" % (t.get_text(), d.width, d.height, sub.sum()))\\n\", \"path\": \"/tmp/check_blit3.py\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_v4i33NUYsrfJEUUd96tU7912", "ui": {"group": null, "chip": "name", "summary": "", "preview": {"keys": ["✎path", "content"], "mode": "content"}, "header": "✓ wrote {path}", "form": "block", "body": "diff", "collapse": "long", "highlight": "", "chrome": "accent", "mutates": true, "undo": true}, "path_arg": "path"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1793178088.2976482, "id": "89fce6f39cf8", "tool_call_id": "call_00_v4i33NUYsrfJEUUd96tU7912", "content": "OK: wrote /tmp/check_blit3.py (2013 chars)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a//tmp/check_blit3.py\n+++ b//tmp/check_blit3.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@\n+import os, sys, runpy\n+import matplotlib\n+matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n+import numpy as np\n+import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n+import matplotlib.animation as manim\n+\n+sys.path.insert(0, os.getcwd())\n+plt.show = lambda *a, **k: None\n+manim.FuncAnimation = type(\"Cap\", (manim.FuncAnimation,), {})\n+\n+g = runpy.run_path(\"scripts/visualize_target.py\", run_name=\"__main__\")\n+fig, update, n = g[\"fig\"], g[\"update\"], g[\"N_FRAMES\"]\n+moving, axw, axa, axi = g[\"moving\"], g[\"ax_world\"], g[\"ax_armor\"], g[\"ax_image\"]\n+\n+\n+def buf():\n+    return np.asarray(fig.canvas.buffer_rgba())[..., :3].astype(int)\n+\n+\n+update(0)\n+fig.canvas.draw()\n+bg = fig.canvas.copy_from_bbox(fig.bbox)\n+\n+i = 200\n+update(i)\n+fig.canvas.draw()\n+full = buf()\n+fig.canvas.restore_region(bg)\n+for a in moving:\n+    a.axes.draw_artist(a)\n+fig.canvas.blit(fig.bbox)\n+blitted = buf()\n+mask = np.abs(blitted - full).max(-1) > 8\n+ys, xs = np.nonzero(mask)\n+print(\"differing pixels:\", mask.sum())\n+print(\"bbox rows %d..%d  cols %d..%d  (image %dx%d)\"\n+      % (ys.min(), ys.max(), xs.min(), xs.max(), full.shape[1], full.shape[0]))\n+for name, ax in ((\"world\", axw), (\"armor\", axa), (\"image\", axi)):\n+    bb = ax.get_window_extent().padded(10)\n+    h = full.shape[0]\n+    lo_y, hi_y = int(h - bb.y1), int(h - bb.y0)\n+    sub = mask[max(lo_y, 0):hi_y, max(int(bb.x0), 0):int(bb.x1)]\n+    print(\"  %-6s window rows %d..%d cols %d..%d -> %d diff px\"\n+          % (name, lo_y, hi_y, int(bb.x0), int(bb.x1), sub.sum()))\n+\n+# where are the texts in the world panel?\n+for t in axw.texts:\n+    d = t.get_window_extent()\n+    h = full.shape[0]\n+    sub = mask[int(h - d.y1) - 2:int(h - d.y0) + 2, int(d.x0) - 2:int(d.x1) + 2]\n+    print(\"  text %-2s at %4.0f,%4.0f size %2.0fx%2.0f -> %d diff px\"\n+          % (t.get_text(), d.x0, h - d.y0, d.width, d.height, sub.sum()))\n+for t in axi.texts:\n+    d = t.get_window_extent()\n+    h = full.shape[0]\n+    sub = mask[int(h - d.y1) - 2:int(h - d.y0) + 2, int(d.x0) - 2:int(d.x1) + 2]\n+    print(\"  tag  %-3s size %2.0fx%2.0f -> %d diff px\" % (t.get_text(), d.width, d.height, sub.sum()))\n"}
