{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1793178208.1927438, "id": "896a5c1a0b1e", "content": "即使使用干净背景，差异仍然存在（第 0 帧也是），这说明问题属于渲染差异，而不是残影。我来定位差异具体在哪里。", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_GIlQRL3KnI8Iq70M9mNQ2849", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Where exactly do the blitted and fully drawn frames disagree?\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport os\\nimport runpy\\nimport sys\\nimport time\\n\\nimport matplotlib\\nmatplotlib.use(\\\"Agg\\\")\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\\nsys.path.insert(0, os.getcwd())\\nplt.show = lambda *a, **k: None\\n\\ng = runpy.run_path(\\\"scripts/visualize_target.py\\\", run_name=\\\"__main__\\\")\\nfig, update = g[\\\"fig\\\"], g[\\\"update\\\"]\\nn, moving, ani = g[\\\"N_FRAMES\\\"], g[\\\"moving\\\"], g[\\\"animation\\\"]\\nseconds, axes = g[\\\"SECONDS\\\"], (g[\\\"ax_world\\\"], g[\\\"ax_armor\\\"], g[\\\"ax_image\\\"])\\n\\n\\ndef buf():\\n    return np.asarray(fig.canvas.buffer_rgba())[..., :3].astype(int)\\n\\n\\ndef snap(i):\\n    update(i)\\n    saved = [a.get_animated() for a in moving]\\n    for a in moving:\\n        a.set_animated(False)\\n    fig.canvas.draw()\\n    out = buf()\\n    for a, was in zip(moving, saved):\\n        a.set_animated(was)\\n    return out\\n\\n\\ndef step(i):\\n    g[\\\"start\\\"] = time.perf_counter() - (i + 0.5) * seconds / n\\n    ani._step()\\n    return buf()\\n\\n\\nfig.canvas.draw()\\ni = 0\\nblit, full = step(i), snap(i)\\nd = np.abs(blit - full).max(-1)\\nbad = d > 8\\nys, xs = np.where(bad)\\nprint(\\\"frame %d: %d px differ, x %d..%d, y %d..%d\\\"\\n      % (i, bad.sum(), xs.min(), xs.max(), ys.min(), ys.max()))\\nfor name, ax in zip((\\\"world\\\", \\\"armor\\\", \\\"image\\\"), axes):\\n    b = ax.bbox\\n    m = bad[int(b.y0):int(b.y1), int(b.x0):int(b.x1)]\\n    print(\\\"  %-5s bbox x %4d..%4d y %4d..%4d  %5d px differ (%.2f%% of axes)\\\"\\n          % (name, b.x0, b.x1, b.y0, b.y1, m.sum(),\\n             100.0 * m.mean()))\\ncols = np.bincount(xs)\\nprint(\\\"columns with hits:\\\", np.where(cols)[0].min(), np.where(cols)[0].max(),\\n      \\\"distinct columns:\\\", (cols > 0).sum())\\nfor k in range(0, len(ys), max(1, len(ys) // 8)):\\n    y, x = ys[k], xs[k]\\n    print(\\\"  (%4d,%4d) full=%s blit=%s\\\" % (x, y, full[y, x], blit[y, x]))\\n\", \"path\": \"/tmp/check_blit5.py\"}"}], "reasoning": "Interesting! Diffs persist even with a clean background, and at frame 0 too. So it's not a ghost — it's a systematic difference in how the image panel is drawn. Rows 212–315 only = image panel band. Diff 0.75% of the whole figure at frame 0 with the same data.\n\nHmm, so something about the image panel blitting differs fundamentally. Perhaps: the `Polygon` fill with alpha 0.35 — when drawn in full draw, patches are composited... hmm same.\n\nWait — maybe the difference is the axes patch/background: `draw_artist` on the fills draws over the restored image, but is the *background* correct? At frame 0, full redraw and blit both should contain the same static stuff.\n\nHold on: `_blit_cache` background covers `ax.bbox`. When we blit, region restored then artists drawn. If the background cache was taken with the artists already drawn (dirty) — in \"clean bg\" test we cleared the cache and redrew with artists hidden, so cache should be clean. Yet diff persists and is the *same magnitude*.\n\nSo maybe the diff is not the background but the artists themselves: 0.75% of figure area... how big is the diff region? rows 212-315, and how many columns? Let me get more detail: count per panel. The image panel occupies roughly x from ~1000 to 1560? figure 16.5x5.2 in at dpi 100 → 1650x520 px. So the image panel is roughly x 1050-1560 (subplot 3). Rows 212-315 ≈ 100 rows. Total diff px = 0.0075*1650*520 ≈ 6400 px. So the diff is much larger than the armor quads.\n\nHmm, 6400 px within rows 212-315 across... maybe all three panels' artists? The 3D panels are full height, though. rows 212-315 only → in 3D panels? The plots are drawn in a band? Actually the 3D panels' content is in the middle vertically ~ rows 100-450.\n\nWait, maybe the differing pixels are the *background* of the image axes: the axes' patch fill (white) vs something? No.\n\nLet me diagnose properly: dump the diff bbox and per-column histogram, and save the full/blit images as PNGs to inspect. Better: figure out what's at those pixels. Print unique colors in full vs blit at diff locations.\n\nHypothesis: alpha compositing! The fill patches (alpha=0.35) — in full draw, the renderer is Agg with `figure.facecolor` etc. When we `draw_artist` the Polygon onto an already-rendered buffer via blit, the Agg renderer... `draw_artist` creates a renderer via `ax.figure.canvas.get_renderer()` and draws onto the figure's `_renderer` buffer? Yes — CanvasAgg caches `self._renderer` and draw_artist uses `renderer` = `self.get_renderer()`, so it draws directly onto the existing buffer. Alpha compositing there should be identical to a full draw.\n\nUnless... `CanvasAgg.draw()` does `self.renderer.clear()` then draws. Fine.\n\nAnother thought: `ax_image.grid(alpha=0.3)`. The grid lines behind fills... same.\n\nHmm, but wait: In full draw with the artists' `animated=False`, `Axes.draw` draws in zorder order including the patch. In blit, patch drawn first, then... same.\n\nLet me look at actual pixel values to identify. Print, for the diff region, a few differing pixel coordinates with RGB values in both.\n\nAlso possible: the *image panel* in the full draw is clipped differently — fills are patches added via `ax.add_patch` with clip to axes; `draw_artist` also clips. Fine.\n\nAnother possibility: labels/tick text? rows 212-315 could be the x-axis tick labels? No, those are at the bottom (~row 470).\n\nLet me just get diagnostics. Also count diff pixels per panel region to see which panels are involved."}
{"type": "tool_call", "timestamp": 1793178208.1927204, "id": "16eda161d5e1", "name": "write_file", "arguments": "{\"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Where exactly do the blitted and fully drawn frames disagree?\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport os\\nimport runpy\\nimport sys\\nimport time\\n\\nimport matplotlib\\nmatplotlib.use(\\\"Agg\\\")\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\\nsys.path.insert(0, os.getcwd())\\nplt.show = lambda *a, **k: None\\n\\ng = runpy.run_path(\\\"scripts/visualize_target.py\\\", run_name=\\\"__main__\\\")\\nfig, update = g[\\\"fig\\\"], g[\\\"update\\\"]\\nn, moving, ani = g[\\\"N_FRAMES\\\"], g[\\\"moving\\\"], g[\\\"animation\\\"]\\nseconds, axes = g[\\\"SECONDS\\\"], (g[\\\"ax_world\\\"], g[\\\"ax_armor\\\"], g[\\\"ax_image\\\"])\\n\\n\\ndef buf():\\n    return np.asarray(fig.canvas.buffer_rgba())[..., :3].astype(int)\\n\\n\\ndef snap(i):\\n    update(i)\\n    saved = [a.get_animated() for a in moving]\\n    for a in moving:\\n        a.set_animated(False)\\n    fig.canvas.draw()\\n    out = buf()\\n    for a, was in zip(moving, saved):\\n        a.set_animated(was)\\n    return out\\n\\n\\ndef step(i):\\n    g[\\\"start\\\"] = time.perf_counter() - (i + 0.5) * seconds / n\\n    ani._step()\\n    return buf()\\n\\n\\nfig.canvas.draw()\\ni = 0\\nblit, full = step(i), snap(i)\\nd = np.abs(blit - full).max(-1)\\nbad = d > 8\\nys, xs = np.where(bad)\\nprint(\\\"frame %d: %d px differ, x %d..%d, y %d..%d\\\"\\n      % (i, bad.sum(), xs.min(), xs.max(), ys.min(), ys.max()))\\nfor name, ax in zip((\\\"world\\\", \\\"armor\\\", \\\"image\\\"), axes):\\n    b = ax.bbox\\n    m = bad[int(b.y0):int(b.y1), int(b.x0):int(b.x1)]\\n    print(\\\"  %-5s bbox x %4d..%4d y %4d..%4d  %5d px differ (%.2f%% of axes)\\\"\\n          % (name, b.x0, b.x1, b.y0, b.y1, m.sum(),\\n             100.0 * m.mean()))\\ncols = np.bincount(xs)\\nprint(\\\"columns with hits:\\\", np.where(cols)[0].min(), np.where(cols)[0].max(),\\n      \\\"distinct columns:\\\", (cols > 0).sum())\\nfor k in range(0, len(ys), max(1, len(ys) // 8)):\\n    y, x = ys[k], xs[k]\\n    print(\\\"  (%4d,%4d) full=%s blit=%s\\\" % (x, y, full[y, x], blit[y, x]))\\n\", \"path\": \"/tmp/check_blit5.py\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_GIlQRL3KnI8Iq70M9mNQ2849", "ui": {"group": null, "chip": "name", "summary": "", "preview": {"keys": ["✎path", "content"], "mode": "content"}, "header": "✓ wrote {path}", "form": "block", "body": "diff", "collapse": "long", "highlight": "", "chrome": "accent", "mutates": true, "undo": true}, "path_arg": "path"}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1793178208.2122607, "id": "63fe584afaea", "tool_call_id": "call_00_GIlQRL3KnI8Iq70M9mNQ2849", "content": "OK: wrote /tmp/check_blit5.py (1774 chars)", "is_error": false, "diff": "--- a//tmp/check_blit5.py\n+++ b//tmp/check_blit5.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@\n+\"\"\"Where exactly do the blitted and fully drawn frames disagree?\"\"\"\n+import os\n+import runpy\n+import sys\n+import time\n+\n+import matplotlib\n+matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n+import numpy as np\n+import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n+\n+sys.path.insert(0, os.getcwd())\n+plt.show = lambda *a, **k: None\n+\n+g = runpy.run_path(\"scripts/visualize_target.py\", run_name=\"__main__\")\n+fig, update = g[\"fig\"], g[\"update\"]\n+n, moving, ani = g[\"N_FRAMES\"], g[\"moving\"], g[\"animation\"]\n+seconds, axes = g[\"SECONDS\"], (g[\"ax_world\"], g[\"ax_armor\"], g[\"ax_image\"])\n+\n+\n+def buf():\n+    return np.asarray(fig.canvas.buffer_rgba())[..., :3].astype(int)\n+\n+\n+def snap(i):\n+    update(i)\n+    saved = [a.get_animated() for a in moving]\n+    for a in moving:\n+        a.set_animated(False)\n+    fig.canvas.draw()\n+    out = buf()\n+    for a, was in zip(moving, saved):\n+        a.set_animated(was)\n+    return out\n+\n+\n+def step(i):\n+    g[\"start\"] = time.perf_counter() - (i + 0.5) * seconds / n\n+    ani._step()\n+    return buf()\n+\n+\n+fig.canvas.draw()\n+i = 0\n+blit, full = step(i), snap(i)\n+d = np.abs(blit - full).max(-1)\n+bad = d > 8\n+ys, xs = np.where(bad)\n+print(\"frame %d: %d px differ, x %d..%d, y %d..%d\"\n+      % (i, bad.sum(), xs.min(), xs.max(), ys.min(), ys.max()))\n+for name, ax in zip((\"world\", \"armor\", \"image\"), axes):\n+    b = ax.bbox\n+    m = bad[int(b.y0):int(b.y1), int(b.x0):int(b.x1)]\n+    print(\"  %-5s bbox x %4d..%4d y %4d..%4d  %5d px differ (%.2f%% of axes)\"\n+          % (name, b.x0, b.x1, b.y0, b.y1, m.sum(),\n+             100.0 * m.mean()))\n+cols = np.bincount(xs)\n+print(\"columns with hits:\", np.where(cols)[0].min(), np.where(cols)[0].max(),\n+      \"distinct columns:\", (cols > 0).sum())\n+for k in range(0, len(ys), max(1, len(ys) // 8)):\n+    y, x = ys[k], xs[k]\n+    print(\"  (%4d,%4d) full=%s blit=%s\" % (x, y, full[y, x], blit[y, x]))\n"}
