in the script that made a text land at a giant pixel coordinate?** The user said earlier that adding `v`/`a` (100 m trajectory) gives \"小黑点\". Now this crash. Both are consistent with: **after they added motion, some text is placed at a huge pixel position** → FreeType delta huge → raster overflow.\n\nWhich text could be at a huge pixel position?\n- `Text3D` labels: `Text3D.draw` → `self.set_position((proj[0][0], proj[1][0]))` then `Text.draw` with transform = the axes' transData. If the 3D axes has xlim/ylim = ±50 (the big cube) and the projected coordinate is, e.g., in *data* space (say -50..50), then the display coordinate is within the axes → fine.\n  \n  BUT what if `Text3D`'s transform is `IdentityTransform` (i.e., x,y used directly as *pixels*) — then `proj[0][0]` (a data-ish coordinate like 30 or -50) becomes a *pixel* coordinate → text drawn at pixel (-50, 30) or (30, 30) → off-figure but not giant.\n\nHmm, that gives wrong positions, not overflow.\n\n- What if the 3D projection yields huge values? If `axes.M` is degenerate... With limits ±50 m and `set_box_aspect((1,1,1))`, fine.\n\n- The image-panel tags: position (u[m].mean(), v[m].mean()) with u up to 7900 → in *data* coords. The axes xlim = [mean-147, mean+147] = ~[3214,3508]. So the tag at u=7900 maps outside the axes box → display coordinate far outside, e.g. x ≈ 1170 + (7900-3214)/294*390 ≈ 1170 + 6200 = 7300 px. That's fine (7300 px). Hmm, but consider *before* the user changed anything: window center = mean, tags near mean → inside.\n\nBut NOW, what if the user applied my suggestion to center the window on the optical axis (u0=640) while keeping the 100 m trajectory? Then the window is [493, 787] and the tags at u up to 7900 → display x = 1187 + (7900-493)/294*390 ≈ 1187 + 9826 = 11013 px. Still not giant. And 11013*64 = 704k — fine.\n\nHmm, so a huge pixel coordinate seems unlikely to be the cause unless something is NaN/1e300.\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe `size` is the problem. `size = prop.get_size_in_points()` — the *font size in points*. If `mtext`'s fontsize were huge... In our script: `ax_image.text(0, 0, f\"A{m}\", fontsize=8)`; `text3d(ax, label)` → `ax.text(0,0,0,label,fontsize=8)`; titles default 12; tick labels 10.\n\nHmm, none.\n\nBUT WAIT: `axes3d` sets the *z-axis label* etc. And for 3D axes, the *offset text*? Hmm, 3D axes have `ax.zaxis` with labels drawn as Text objects whose positions come from the 3D projection: `axis3d.Axis.draw` sets `self.label.set_position(...)`? In `axis3d.Axis._get_axis_line_edge_points` and `draw`:\n\n```python\n    def draw(self, renderer):\n        ...\n        # Draw axis lines, ticks, tick labels\n        ...\n        self.label.draw(renderer)\n```\nAnd tick labels' positions are computed via `proj3d` with `self.axes.M`. If the projection is degenerate, tick label positions could be NaN/huge.\n\n**Crucially**: with a huge (100 m) 3D cube AND `set_box_aspect((1,1,1))`, is the projection degenerate? No.\n\nHmm, but what about the **`DISTANCE=3` + 100 m trajectory + the 3D axes with zlim spanning 100 m**... The `Axes3D.get_proj` uses the *box aspect* and the limits; a 100 m cube is fine.\n\nHmm, hmm. But wait: what if the user changed the world panel limits to a fixed arena (my suggestion 1–4 in the previous turn)? In chat mode they can't have me edit, but they might have edited themselves. If `ax_world.set_xlim(-1, 9)` etc. then fine.\n\nLet me step back and consider the *first* report of this error (at conversation start). At that time the script was a \"before\" version. The traceback shows `_draw_text_glyphs_and_boxes` → `_render_glyph`. In that version, was there motion? The summary says the script had `DISTANCE=3, HEIGHT=0.5, RADIUS=0.3, YAW=0, CAM_YAW=0, FX=800, SECONDS=10, FPS=60` and the scene was static translation?? Hmm, the summary says `track = TargetMotion()(...)` with `yaw_rate=3.0` and `mode=\"complex\"` — no v/a. So no huge coordinates then either. And yet the same crash happened. So the crash is N