{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1793188154.1814363, "id": "060f606b7305", "tool_call_id": "call_00_84JV1jXNBIcGo3g37e165148", "content": "OK: command succeeded\nstdout:\n22:        t_e = t.unsqueeze(-1)\n25:        sinus_amp = _get(\"sinus_amp\", (bsz, 3))\n27:        rw_sigma = _get(\"rw_sigma\", (bsz, 3))\n29:        pos = p0.unsqueeze(1)\n31:        if sinus_amp.abs().sum() > 0:\n32:            pos = pos + sinus_amp.unsqueeze(1) * torch.sin(\n36:        if rw_sigma.abs().sum() > 0:\n37:            increments = torch.randn(\n39:            ) * rw_sigma.unsqueeze(1)\n40:            pos = pos + torch.cumsum(increments, dim=1)\n167:        body_pos = body[\"positions\"]\n", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "tool_result", "timestamp": 1793188154.1926064, "id": "e4f1cf6d6b33", "tool_call_id": "call_01_hL6zoYIKPgeUwSws2VCP0478", "content": "OK: command succeeded\nstdout:\n        )\n        # facing direction of each plate: local +Z is the plate normal\n        normal_local = torch.tensor([0.0, 0.0, 1.0], device=device, dtype=radius.dtype)\n        world_normal = torch.einsum(\"btmij,j->btmi\", world_rot, normal_local)\n        armor_yaws = torch.atan2(world_normal[..., 1], world_normal[..., 0])\n\n        return {\n            \"corners\": corners,\n            \"centers\": centers,\n            \"armor_yaws\": armor_yaws,\n            \"armor_rotations\": world_rot,\n            \"body_positions\": body_pos,\n            \"body_rotations\": body_rot,\n        }\n", "is_error": false, "diff": ""}
{"type": "assistant_message", "timestamp": 1793188166.2308567, "id": "a74a20c2dedb", "content": "## 原因：`positions` 的时间维只在 `sinus`（或随机游走）分支里才会被\"撑开\"\n\n`diff_env/target.py:29-40`：\n\n```python\n29:  pos = p0.unsqueeze(1)                          # (bsz, 1, 3)  ← 只有 1 帧\n31:  if sinus_amp.abs().sum() > 0:\n32:      pos = pos + sinus_amp.unsqueeze(1) * torch.sin(...)   # 广播成 (bsz, sln, 3)\n36:  if rw_sigma.abs().sum() > 0:\n40:      pos = pos + torch.cumsum(increments, dim=1)           # 同样广播成 (bsz, sln, 3)\n```\n\n`pos` 初始只有 **1 帧**（`p0.unsqueeze(1)`），它变成 `sln` 帧长，完全依赖后面两个 `if` 里的加法广播。\n\n把 `sinus_amp` / `sinus_freq` 注释掉后：\n\n- `_get(\"sinus_amp\", ...)` 返回全 0 → `sinus_amp.abs().sum() > 0` 为 **False** → 第 31 行的分支跳过；\n- `rw_sigma` 你没传 → 也是全 0 → 第 36 行的分支同样跳过。\n\n于是 `pos` 停在 `(1, 1, 3)`，一路原样返回（`target.py:191` 的 `\"body_positions\": body_pos`）。\n\n脚本这边：\n\n```python\n126:  body_pos = track[\"body_positions\"][0].numpy()    # (1, 3)  ← 不是 (6000, 3)!\n183:  place(world_frames[2], body_pos[index], body_rot[index])\n```\n\n`body_pos` 的第 0 维长度是 **1**，所以 `body_pos[6]` 立刻越界，报的正是 `axis 0 with size 1`。\n\n## 为什么第一次崩在 index 6，第二次在 8\n\n`animate()` 用墙上时钟算帧号（`scripts/visualize_target.py:212-214`）：\n\n```python\nindex = min(int((time.perf_counter() - start) / SECONDS * N_FRAMES), N_FRAMES - 1)\n```\n\n`SECONDS=100`、`N_FRAMES=6000` → 每秒 60 帧。`start` 在模块级记录，而建图 + `FuncAnimation` 初始化大约花了 0.1 s，所以**第一次真正 draw 时 index 已经是 6**；窗口 resize 触发第二次 `_init_draw` 时又过了 0.03 s → index 8。所以 6 和 8 只是\"初始化耗时\"的数字，跟运动本身无关。\n\n## 为什么 `centers` / `corners` / `body_rot` 不报错\n\n只有 `pos` 退化，其它都由 `t` 直接生成：\n\n```python\n173:  centers = body_pos.unsqueeze(2) + torch.einsum(\"btij,bmj->btmi\", body_rot, local_pos)\n```\n\n`body_pos` 的 `(1,1,3)` 变成 `(1,1,1,3)`，与 `(1,6000,4,3)` 相加时**广播**成 `(1,6000,4,3)`，所以 `corners`、`centers` 是正确的 6000 帧。`body_rot` 由 `euler_to_rotmat(yaw, pitch, roll)` 从 `t` 算出，本来就是 `(1,6000,3,3)`。\n\n也就是说：**三个面板里板和坐标架的姿态都正常，唯独你新加的 `body_positions` 是个 1 帧的数组。** 这也解释了为什么之前用 `centers.mean(1)` 的写法没暴露这个问题——`centers` 被广播好了。\n\n## 修法：在 `BodyMotion` 里一开始就把时间维展开\n\n`diff_env/target.py:29`：\n\n```python\npos = p0.unsqueeze(1).expand(-1, sln, -1)     # 任何分支不执行时也是 (bsz, sln, 3)\n```\n\n（`expand` 返回的是视图，但第 32/40 行都是 `pos = pos + ...` 新建张量，不会就地改写，安全。如果你更想避免视图语义，用 `p0.unsqueeze(1).repeat(1, sln, 1)`。）\n\n改完之后：\n\n- `sinus` 注释掉 → `pos` 仍是 `(1,6000,3)`，`body_pos[index]` 正常；\n- `sinus` 打开 → 结果不变；\n- `mode=\"static\"`、`rw_sigma` 单独开启等所有组合都一致。\n\n## 为什么值得在模型里修，而不是在脚本里兜\n\n现在 `positions` 的形状**取决于哪个运动分支被执行**：开 `sinus` 是 `(bsz, sln, 3)`，全关是 `(bsz, 1, 3)`。任何下游代码（可视化、损失、日志）都得先猜分支，这就是这次崩溃的根源。在 `pos` 创建处一次性定型，契约就稳定了。\n\n一句验证（work 模式）：\n\n```python\nprint(track[\"body_positions\"].shape)     # 应为 (1, 6000, 3)\n```\n\n（以上为只读分析；改 `diff_env/target.py` 或脚本需要切到 **work 模式**。）", "tool_calls": [], "reasoning": "Confirmed. Now the answer:\n\nRoot cause: `pos` is only ever expanded to the time dimension by the sinus / random-walk branches. With sinus commented out (sinus_amp defaults to 0) and rw_sigma unset (0), neither branch runs, so `pos` stays `(bsz, 1, 3)`.\n\nThen in the script, `body_pos = track[\"body_positions\"][0].numpy()` → shape (1, 3), so `body_pos[6]` → IndexError size 1.\n\nWhy only from index 6: wall-clock indexing; ~0.1 s of startup → 6 frames at 60 fps.\n\nWhy centers/corners are fine: broadcasting at line 173-174.\n\nFix: line 29 → `pos = p0.unsqueeze(1).expand(-1, sln, -1)` (or repeat).\n\nAlso note the derivative issues: `torch.stack`? no.\n\nAlso mention verification: print shapes.\n\nAlso mention: it's not just about body_positions — any code consuming `positions` gets a shape that depends on which branch fired; that's a fragile contract, fix at the source.\n\nAlso worth noting: `center` derived `centers.mean(1)` (my earlier A suggestion) would have worked even now, because `centers` is broadcast to full length — that's why the error only shows with the B fix. Good detail: option A (mean) is resilient to this bug; option B (positions) exposes a latent bug in BodyMotio